 foreign ministers go to speak  with the leadership in the opposition  that's fine absolutely normally but in  fact they go right into the heart of  political events - an event that is  conducted against the existing rules  governing demonstrations taking part in  these events is and excuse me for saying  this a very simple case of interference  in another nations internal affairs  President Yanukovych has insisted he  does eventually want to see Ukraine  build closer ties with its European  neighbors but with ill-feeling reaching  an all-time high and neither side  showing any sign of backing down this is  a crisis which could get far worse Chris  Wade sky news
 

